		<row>
			<c>
				<c>
					<f>3</f>
					<tl/>
				</c>
			</c>
		</row>
	</rowsItem>
	<rowsItem>
		<index>52</index>
		<row>
			<c>
				<c>
					<f>2</f>
					<tl>
						<v8:item>
							<v8:lang>ru</v8:lang>
							<v8:content>Fixed and intangible assets</v8:content>
						</v8:item>
					</tl>
				</c>
			</c>
		</row>
	</rowsItem>
	<rowsItem>
		<index>53</index>
		<row>
			<c>
				<c>
					<f>4</f>
					<tl>
						<v8:item>
							<v8:lang>ru</v8:lang>
							<v8:content>The following fixed asset accounting features are improved:</v8:content>
						</v8:item>
					</tl>
				</c>
			</c>
		</row>
	</rowsItem>
	<rowsItem>
		<index>54</index>
		<row>
			<c>
				<c>
					<f>4</f>
					<tl>
						<v8:item>
							<v8:lang>ru</v8:lang>
							<v8:content>The selection method of posting options in accounting has changed in document forms.
Filling in the preliminary cost is now not always necessary, and it can exceed the actual cost.
The "Adjust fixed asset cost and depreciation" document takes into account appreciation, revaluation, partial write-off, splitting, and merge when calculating depreciation.
You can record cost increase due to additional costs that are not related to appreciation.
Upon recognition, you can include in the cost expenses received before the end of the month.
Fixed assets — Physical inventory and Intangible assets — Physical inventory are added.
And other.</v8:content>
						</v8:item>
					</tl>
				</c>
			</c>
		</row>
	</rowsItem>
